export const SITE_SEARCH_CORPUS: SiteSearchDoc[] = [
  {"href":"/cloud","title":"Cloud & Servers","category":"Page · Cloud","description":"CloudHost247 cloud and servers: VPS, public and private cloud, dedicated and enterprise servers, operating systems, network, monitoring, firewalls and backups.","body":"Cloud & Servers CloudHost247 cloud and servers: VPS, public and private cloud, dedicated and enterprise servers, operating systems, network, monitoring, firewalls and backups. Pick the shape of the machine Compute VPS Hosting Guaranteed virtual resources with full administrative access, on shared hardware. Public Cloud Elastic compute that can be resized as demand changes. Private Cloud Isolated capacity reserved for a single tenant. Dedicated Servers An entire physical machine, with no neighbour. Enterprise Servers High-capacity configurations for serious workloads. Game Servers Low-latency hosting for multiplayer communities. Everything around the machine Operations Operating Systems The catalogue available at provisioning time. Infrastructure Regions, facilities and how the network fits together. Monitoring Telemetry and alerts on the resources you run. Firewalls Rule-based network filtering per server. Backups Scheduled jobs with a restorable history. IP Management Addresses, reverse DNS and floating IPs. What is on this page is what the platform can provision"},
  {"href":"/cloud/public","title":"Public Cloud","category":"Page · Cloud","description":"Elastic public cloud instances from CloudHost247: resize compute as demand changes, with the OS catalogue, network controls and monitoring included.","body":"Public Cloud Elastic public cloud instances from CloudHost247: resize compute as demand changes, with the OS catalogue, network controls and monitoring included. Elastic where it matters Why public cloud Resize without rebuilding Move to a larger or smaller instance shape as the workload changes, rather than migrating to a new product. Fast provisioning Instances are created from a configured image, so a working server exists in minutes rather than days. Your choice of operating system Provision from the catalogue of operating systems the platform holds images for. Network control Firewall rules and private addressing so the instance is only reachable where it should be. Persistence Attached storage survives a rebuild of the instance, which is what makes resizing safe. Monitoring built in Resource telemetry is collected so capacity decisions are made from data rather than from an alert at 03:00. Public cloud instances on this deployment Live pricing Region availability is configuration, not a claim"},
  {"href":"/cloud/private","title":"Private Cloud","category":"Page · Cloud","description":"Private cloud from CloudHost247: isolated compute capacity reserved for one tenant, for workloads that cannot share hardware with anyone else.","body":"Private Cloud Private cloud from CloudHost247: isolated compute capacity reserved for one tenant, for workloads that cannot share hardware with anyone else. What isolation actually changes The boundary No noisy neighbours Performance is not affected by another tenant's load, because there is no other tenant on the same resources. A smaller blast radius Isolation is a security property as well as a performance one: there is no shared host to be reached through. Easier to explain A defined boundary is far easier to describe in a compliance or customer questionnaire than shared hosting is. Your stack Choose the operating system and configuration the workload needs, rather than working around a fixed image. Network under your control Addressing, firewall rules and connectivity designed around the application. Managed if you want it Operate it yourself, or have the CloudHost247 team run the platform layer for you. Private cloud capacity on this deployment Live pricing Private cloud is scoped, not self-service"},
  {"href":"/cloud/enterprise-servers","title":"Enterprise Servers","category":"Page · Servers","description":"Enterprise-grade server configurations from CloudHost247 for high-capacity workloads, with redundancy options, managed operations and provider-backed hardware.","body":"Enterprise Servers Enterprise-grade server configurations from CloudHost247 for high-capacity workloads, with redundancy options, managed operations and provider-backed hardware. What changes at this level Sizing up Sized to the workload Configurations are chosen around measured requirements — core count, memory, storage throughput — rather than a fixed tier. Built for data-heavy services The configuration that makes a database host viable: fast storage, memory for working sets, and cores for concurrency. A platform under other services When a host runs virtualisation or containers, its failure footprint is larger — so resilience is designed in. Monitored as critical Telemetry, alerting and capacity tracking so limits are seen before they become incidents. Managed operations Patch management, hardening and hands-on administration available as part of the service. Backups and recovery Backup jobs sized to the data volume, with a restore plan that has been agreed rather than improvised. Quoted against requirements, not published as a price"},
  {"href":"/cloud/game-servers","title":"Game Servers","category":"Page · Servers","description":"Low-latency game server hosting from CloudHost247 with the compute to hold a community, DDoS-path filtering and full administrative access.","body":"Game Servers Low-latency game server hosting from CloudHost247 with the compute to hold a community, DDoS-path filtering and full administrative access. The things that actually matter What a game server needs Latency first Placement and network path matter more than raw clock speed. The region is chosen to sit near the players. Protection against floods Game servers are a favourite target for traffic floods. Network-level filtering is part of the service, not an upsell. Full access Root or administrator access, so you install and configure the game stack the way the community expects. Compute that holds a population Player counts, plugins and world size drive requirements. Configurations are sized for the community you actually run. World data protected Scheduled backups of the game data, because a corrupted world file is an unrecoverable community. Monitored Telemetry on CPU, memory and network so a growth problem shows up before players notice it."},
  {"href":"/cloud/infrastructure","title":"Infrastructure","category":"Page · Infrastructure","description":"How CloudHost247 infrastructure is organised: providers, regions, network, storage and the operational layer that runs customer services.","body":"Infrastructure How CloudHost247 infrastructure is organised: providers, regions, network, storage and the operational layer that runs customer services. How the layers stack Architecture Facilities and providers Compute and network are delivered from data centres operated by infrastructure providers, chosen per region and recorded in the platform. Network Public addressing, firewalling and private networking sit between the facility and your service, configured per server. Control layer Provisioning, operating-system images, DNS, certificates, backups and monitoring are owned by the platform rather than by hand. Reconciliation The platform continuously compares what it believes is provisioned against what the provider reports, so drift is detected rather than discovered. Observability Server telemetry, service state and operation logs feed the same account view you use. Isolation Services are separated at the platform layer, and access to provider credentials is restricted and audited. What this page will not tell you Honesty A list of cities Regions exist only when a provider is configured for them. The data centres page shows what is genuinely configured in your deployment — no decorative world map. An uptime percentage A published percentage that does not come from measured, customer-visible monitoring would be a number we invented. Service status shows what the platform can verify right now. Certifications we do not hold Certification claims require an audit report with a name and a date. We publish none we cannot produce."},
  {"href":"/cloud/data-centers","title":"Data Centers","category":"Page · Infrastructure","description":"The data centre regions CloudHost247 is configured to deploy into, listed from live configuration rather than a marketing map.","body":"Data Centers The data centre regions CloudHost247 is configured to deploy into, listed from live configuration rather than a marketing map. Regions configured on this deployment Available regions What region choice affects Selecting a region Latency to your users The physical distance between the facility and the people using the service is the single largest factor in response time. Data residency Where data is stored is a legal question as well as a technical one. Region selection is how you answer it. The provider operating the facility Each region names the provider that runs the physical site. Addressing and connectivity IP ranges and the network path are determined by the region the service is deployed into."},
  {"href":"/cloud/network","title":"Network","category":"Page · Infrastructure","description":"The CloudHost247 network layer: public and private addressing, firewall filtering, reverse DNS, floating IPs and the observability that sits on top.","body":"Network The CloudHost247 network layer: public and private addressing, firewall filtering, reverse DNS, floating IPs and the observability that sits on top. What you can control Capabilities IP addressing Public addresses assigned to your service, managed in your account, with the option to move a floating address between servers. Reverse DNS PTR records set correctly, which matters for mail deliverability and for anything that logs connections. Firewall filtering Rules applied in order to allow, deny or rate-limit traffic to a server, with the order visible. Flood mitigation Known-abusive traffic patterns are filtered at the network edge rather than reaching the application. Traffic telemetry Throughput and packet-level signals recorded per service so a change in behaviour is visible as a graph. IPv6 Dual-stack addressing where the region and provider support it. Bandwidth and traffic terms are contractual"},
  {"href":"/cloud/operating-systems","title":"Operating Systems","category":"Page · Platform","description":"The operating system catalogue available when provisioning a server on CloudHost247, including version lifecycles and provider image availability.","body":"Operating Systems The operating system catalogue available when provisioning a server on CloudHost247, including version lifecycles and provider image availability. Facts the platform keeps track of How the catalogue behaves Families and versions Each entry is a specific family, version and architecture rather than a vague name. Lifecycle status End-of-life operating systems are marked, because a server installed today should not be unsupported next year. Provider image availability An operating system is only selectable where the provider in that region actually offers an image for it. Control panels Where a panel is configured to be provisioned on top of an operating system, that mapping is explicit. Administerable Versions, images and availability are configuration, maintained by administrators rather than hardcoded in the application. Supported means patched Operating systems with active vendor security support are the ones worth provisioning; the catalogue shows which those are. If a version is not in the list, it is not provisionable"},
  {"href":"/cloud/server-management","title":"Server Management","category":"Page · Operations","description":"Server management from CloudHost247: provisioning, operating-system lifecycle, monitoring, firewall control, backups, patching and hands-on administration.","body":"Server Management Server management from CloudHost247: provisioning, operating-system lifecycle, monitoring, firewall control, backups, patching and hands-on administration. What the platform does for you Available today Provisioning and rebuilds Create servers from a catalogue image, rebuild them from a known-good state, and record which image each server runs. Access management Administrative access is issued and rotated through the platform, and server credentials are stored encrypted rather than pasted into tickets. Monitoring and alerting Resource telemetry collected per server, with alerting so a saturation event is noticed while it is still an event. Firewall control Rules attached to the server, applied in a defined order, with the effective ruleset visible. Backups Scheduled jobs with a run history and a restore path from your account. Reconciliation and logs The platform compares desired state with provider reality and records every infrastructure operation for audit. Hand the platform layer to us Managed services Patching and hardening Operating system and platform components patched on a schedule, with the changes recorded. Monitoring response Alerts are acted on rather than merely delivered — the difference between monitoring and management. Incident handling A named path for an incident: who is looking, what is being tried, and what customers are told. Change management Changes made deliberately, with a way back, instead of directly on production at 17:55 on a Friday."},
  {"href":"/cloud/monitoring","title":"Monitoring","category":"Page · Operations","description":"Resource monitoring and service telemetry for CloudHost247 servers, applications and hosting, with historical data and alerting you can act on.","body":"Monitoring Resource monitoring and service telemetry for CloudHost247 servers, applications and hosting, with historical data and alerting you can act on. Signals worth keeping What is measured Compute pressure CPU and memory over time, so the difference between a busy day and a capacity problem is visible. Storage growth Disk consumption trending, because a full disk takes a service down quietly and completely. Traffic Throughput in and out, which is where a traffic spike or a leak is first detectable. Service state Whether each service is reachable and answering, recorded as state rather than as a promise. Alerts that mean something Notifications tied to a threshold rather than to every fluctuation, so an alert is worth reading. History Retained telemetry you can go back through when working out when a problem actually started. Why there is no uptime figure on this page"},
  {"href":"/cloud/backups","title":"Server & Cloud Backups","category":"Page · Data","description":"Backup jobs for CloudHost247 servers and applications: scheduled runs, visible history, defined retention and restores performed from your account.","body":"Server & Cloud Backups Backup jobs for CloudHost247 servers and applications: scheduled runs, visible history, defined retention and restores performed from your account. How jobs are managed Mechanics Scheduled runs Backups happen on a schedule attached to the service, not on someone's memory. Scoped per service A server, an application and a hosting account each have their own backup record, so one restore never affects another. What a backup contains Each record states what was captured — files, databases, volumes — so you know what a restore will bring back. Separate storage Backup data is held on storage separate from the live service, so losing a server does not lose its backups. Restore path Restores run against the service, with the selected backup shown before the restore begins. Failure visibility A failed run is recorded as failed, which is the only way to know a backup plan is not quietly doing nothing."},
  {"href":"/cloud/firewall","title":"Firewalls","category":"Page · Security","description":"Rule-based firewall control for CloudHost247 servers: ordered allow, deny and rate-limit rules applied at the network layer, with the effective ruleset visible.","body":"Firewalls Rule-based firewall control for CloudHost247 servers: ordered allow, deny and rate-limit rules applied at the network layer, with the effective ruleset visible. What you can express Control Ordered evaluation Rules are applied in sequence and the order is shown, because order is what determines the outcome. Default deny A policy of closing everything and opening what the service needs is the one that ages well. Rate limiting Limit connections from a source so a brute-force attempt or a runaway client cannot consume the service. Source restrictions Restrict administrative ports to known addresses so SSH is not reachable from the whole internet. Per-service rules Rules are attached to a specific server, so a change is scoped to the thing it was meant for. Auditable changes Rule changes are recorded against your account, which makes an incident review possible."},
  {"href":"/cloud/security","title":"Cloud Security","category":"Page · Security","description":"How CloudHost247 secures cloud services: credential handling, isolation, network control, patch management, logging and incident response.","body":"Cloud Security How CloudHost247 secures cloud services: credential handling, isolation, network control, patch management, logging and incident response. What is enforced Controls Provider credentials Infrastructure provider credentials are stored encrypted, never returned to a browser, and used only by the platform's own operations. Audit trail Infrastructure operations and administrative actions are recorded, so who did what and when is answerable. Role-based access Administrative capability is granted by role and re-verified server-side on every request rather than trusted from the interface. Service isolation Customer services are separated so that one cannot read or control another. Patch management Operating systems and platform components are patched on a schedule, with changes tracked against the service. Incident response A defined path for detection, containment, notification and review — written down before it is needed. Protect your own account Access you control Turn on multi-factor authentication TOTP and passkey authentication are supported. A password alone is the weakest link in any hosting account. Review administrative users Staff and administrative access should be limited to people who need it, and removed when they do not. Keep recovery details current Password recovery and second-factor recovery both depend on the contact details on the account being right."},
  {"href":"/cloud/ip-management","title":"IP Management","category":"Page · Infrastructure","description":"Manage the IP addresses assigned to your CloudHost247 services: public addressing, floating IPs, reverse DNS and the records that tie them to your services.","body":"IP Management Manage the IP addresses assigned to your CloudHost247 services: public addressing, floating IPs, reverse DNS and the records that tie them to your services. What you can do Address management See the assignment Every address shows the service it belongs to, so an audit does not require a spreadsheet. Set reverse DNS PTR records for your addresses, which mail servers and log correlation both depend on. Move an address A floating address can be reassigned to another server, which is what makes failover practical. IPv6 where available Dual-stack assignment where the region and provider support it. Justification for more Additional address requests are assessed against real need, which is what keeps the pool usable for everyone. Abuse handling Addresses reported for abuse are handled under the Acceptable Use Policy, whichever service holds them."},
  {"href":"/cloud/managed-services","title":"Managed Services","category":"Page · Operations","description":"Managed services from CloudHost247: patching, monitoring response, backup verification, firewall changes and hands-on administration, confirmed per plan.","body":"Managed Services Managed services from CloudHost247: patching, monitoring response, backup verification, firewall changes and hands-on administration, confirmed per plan. Work we take over when it is in your plan What management covers Operating-system patching Security updates applied on a schedule for the operating systems we support, with the maintenance window agreed rather than guessed. Monitoring response Alerts that are not just sent but read: when a service you have management on goes down, the alert becomes somebody's job. Backup verification Backup jobs watched and restores tested where the product supports them, because a backup nobody has restored is only a hope. Firewall and access changes Rule changes and access troubleshooting carried out through the platform, so the effective ruleset stays reviewable. Hands-on administration Service configuration, package installation from supported sources and the routine tasks a hosting panel exposes. A record you can read Work is recorded against the service it changed, so you can see what was done and when without asking for a summary. What management is not Confirm before you buy Which operating systems are supported What the maintenance window is Whether restores are performed for you What response times your plan publishes Which applications are in scope How it starts Tell us about the service The plan, the operating system and what the service has to do — a short description is enough to scope it. We confirm the scope in writing What is covered, what is not, and the response expectation. This is the same scope a plan feature or proposal states. It becomes part of the service Ongoing work is recorded against the service, and changes that need your consent are put to you before they happen."},
  {"href":"/developers","title":"Developer Platform","category":"Page · Developers","description":"Developer services on CloudHost247: supported runtimes, deployment records, per-app settings, APIs and docs. Availability follows the live catalogue.","body":"Developer Platform Developer services on CloudHost247: supported runtimes, deployment records, per-app settings, APIs and docs. Availability follows the live catalogue. Pick your stack Runtimes Node.js Long-running services with managed supervision. PHP Single scripts through to full frameworks. Python WSGI and ASGI applications with virtual environments. Laravel Queues, scheduler, storage and deployment. Docker Your own images with persistent volumes. APIs HTTP APIs with TLS, secrets and rate control. Everything around the runtime Platform Deployment Supported application installs and updates, with recorded status, steps and available recovery. Environments Variables, secrets and volumes per application. DNS Zones and records for the services you run. Databases Managed engines your application can connect to. Monitoring Telemetry and alerts on your services. Firewalls Close everything the service does not need. Documentation that matches the platform Written down, not folklore"},
  {"href":"/developers/deployment","title":"Application Deployment","category":"Page · Developers","description":"Operate supported CloudHost247 application installs and updates with deployment status, step events, per-application configuration and recovery where supported.","body":"Application Deployment Operate supported CloudHost247 application installs and updates with deployment status, step events, per-application configuration and recovery where supported. What happens to a supported application The deployment flow Choose a published application Select an application and version that the live marketplace marks as published. The native deployment flow uses that version’s stored manifest. Validate the target The worker checks the application version, target server, supported hosting type and available capacity before provisioning. Provision and record The deployment uses the configured image and resources, then records the operation status, step state and events against the installation. Review the outcome Inspect the deployment record and application logs. If a supported infrastructure step fails, the worker attempts to reverse completed steps and records the result. What the deployment workflow records Properties worth having It is recorded Each operation has a durable status, step states and event history rather than disappearing with a terminal session. Versions are explicit Native deployments use a published application version and its stored manifest; an arbitrary repository commit is not implied. Configuration is separate Application environment values are managed per installation; sensitive values are encrypted in storage and omitted from API responses. Failure is visible A failed operation is recorded with its error and event history. The worker attempts to reverse completed infrastructure steps where it can. Scoped per application Installations and deployment records are linked to the application and server they operate on. Tracked over time The deployment history shows which supported operation ran and when. Git builds and CI are separate capabilities"},
  {"href":"/developers/environments","title":"Application Environments","category":"Page · Developers","description":"Configure CloudHost247 application environments: environment variables and secrets, persistent volumes, per-application domains and certificates.","body":"Application Environments Configure CloudHost247 application environments: environment variables and secrets, persistent volumes, per-application domains and certificates. What lives on the environment Configuration model Environment variables Plain configuration values injected into the process, so the same image runs in different places with different values. Secrets Sensitive values are stored encrypted in the platform, not shown again after saving, and never included in an API response. Volumes Storage declared by the application so data survives a redeploy, a rebuild or a move between hosts. Domains A domain can be attached to the application, with its own certificate, so environments are distinguishable at a glance. Service connections Reference a database or cache the account owns instead of pasting raw hostnames and ports everywhere. Separate per environment Staging and production are separate applications with separate configuration — the only way they can be safely different. Things that keep environments sane Practice Never commit secrets If a credential is in the repository, it is in every clone and every backup of that repository. Rotate it once it has been. Keep environments structurally identical The same services, the same variable names, different values. Divergent structure is what turns a staging pass into a false negative. Give the environment its own domain An address that identifies the environment prevents the classic incident of debugging production while thinking it is staging."},
  {"href":"/developers/nodejs","title":"Node.js Hosting","category":"Page · Developers","description":"Node.js hosting on CloudHost247: review available runtimes and product integrations for process supervision, environment configuration, application logs and domains.","body":"Node.js Hosting Node.js hosting on CloudHost247: review available runtimes and product integrations for process supervision, environment configuration, application logs and domains. The operational parts of a Node app What the platform handles Supervision The process is managed and restarted after a crash, which is what turns a successful test into a running service. Configuration Ports, connection strings and flags supplied as environment variables rather than edited into the source. Logs Standard output and error are captured per application so an unhandled rejection is findable. Deployment Native application deployments install published versions and configured images. Git source builds depend on an enabled control-panel integration. Data services Managed MySQL-compatible, PostgreSQL, MongoDB and Redis services your application connects to. Domains and certificates Attach the hostname the service answers on, and let the certificate be issued for it. Bring your own runtime discipline"},
  {"href":"/developers/php","title":"PHP Hosting","category":"Page · Developers","description":"PHP hosting on CloudHost247: review available runtime versions, Composer, databases and scheduled-task support in the selected hosting product.","body":"PHP Hosting PHP hosting on CloudHost247: review available runtime versions, Composer, databases and scheduled-task support in the selected hosting product. Provided rather than assembled What a PHP app needs Maintained PHP Runtimes that receive security updates, so an old version is a choice rather than an inheritance. Extensions and Composer The extension set applications declare, and Composer to resolve dependencies from the lock file. Scheduled tasks Cron entries for queues, imports and housekeeping, so the scheduled work a framework needs actually runs. OPcache Bytecode caching configured on, because it is the single cheapest performance win in PHP. Databases MySQL-compatible, MariaDB and PostgreSQL services alongside the application. Deployment Use the deployment method available on the selected hosting plan. Native application deployments install published images; source builds depend on a configured control-panel integration. PHP shifts responsibility to the application The honest part Keep the framework current A framework that no longer receives security fixes is the most common cause of a compromised PHP site. Vet what you install Packages run with the application's privileges. A dependency is code you are choosing to run. Use the lock file Deploying without a lock file means deploying whatever the registry serves today — which is not the same thing as what you tested."},
  {"href":"/developers/python","title":"Python Hosting","category":"Page · Developers","description":"Host Python applications on CloudHost247: virtual environments, WSGI and ASGI applications, background workers, scheduled jobs and managed data services.","body":"Python Hosting Host Python applications on CloudHost247: virtual environments, WSGI and ASGI applications, background workers, scheduled jobs and managed data services. What Python needs to run in production The stack Isolated environments Dependencies installed per application, so two applications that disagree about a library version can coexist. WSGI and ASGI Serve synchronous frameworks and asynchronous ones, with TLS and routing in front of the application. Workers Long-running processes for queues and background work, supervised and restarted on failure. Scheduled jobs Cron for periodic work like synchronisation, reporting and cleanup, rather than a process that sleeps. Data services PostgreSQL, MySQL-compatible, MongoDB and Redis services your application connects to. Logs and telemetry Application output and resource use captured per service, so a slow query or a memory leak is visible."},
  {"href":"/developers/laravel","title":"Laravel Hosting","category":"Page · Developers","description":"Laravel hosting on CloudHost247 with the application services a Laravel site may need: queue workers, scheduler jobs, storage and database options.","body":"Laravel Hosting Laravel hosting on CloudHost247 with the application services a Laravel site may need: queue workers, scheduler jobs, storage and database options. The four things that break in production Laravel specifics Queue workers Supervised worker processes so queued jobs are processed and re-started after a deployment or a failure. The scheduler A single cron entry running Laravel's scheduler, so you do not have to remember which tasks need which timing. Writable storage Persistent volumes for uploads and framework storage, so a redeploy does not erase user files. Migrations A database that can be dumped, restored and migrated with a backup taken before the change. Environment configuration The values in .env supplied per environment instead of living in the repository. Logs Application and queue output captured per service, which is where a failing job is actually visible. The sequence that avoids surprises Deploying a Laravel app Back up before migrating Run the database backup first. A failed migration with no backup is a much worse day than a failed migration. Release the new code Deploy from the repository so the release is tied to a revision rather than to a folder someone edited. Restart the workers Queue workers must pick up new code; a supervised worker is restarted by the platform on release."},
  {"href":"/developers/docker","title":"Docker Hosting","category":"Page · Developers","description":"Run Docker containers on CloudHost247: pull from public or private registries, attach persistent volumes, inject configuration and route a domain with TLS.","body":"Docker Hosting Run Docker containers on CloudHost247: pull from public or private registries, attach persistent volumes, inject configuration and route a domain with TLS. What the platform provides Running containers Image deployment Run an image the platform can pull, so the tested artefact is the deployed artefact. Private registries Registry credentials are stored so a private image can be pulled without embedding a token in a script. Volumes State declared by the application lives on a volume, so replacing the container does not destroy data. Configuration Environment variables and secrets applied per application, not baked into the image. Routing Attach the hostname, let the certificate issue, and the container is on the internet the way you intended. Observability Logs, resource use and restart behaviour recorded, so a crash loop is something you can see. Things that make containers safe to run Container hygiene Pin the tag A moving tag means a redeploy can change the application without anyone deciding to change it. Do not run as root by default A container that does not need root should not have it; privileged containers widen the blast radius for no benefit. Keep state on volumes Anything written inside the container filesystem is temporary by definition, whatever it looks like during testing. Choose small base images A smaller image pulls faster, starts faster and presents fewer packages to keep patched."},
  {"href":"/hosting","title":"Hosting","category":"Page · Hosting","description":"Compare CloudHost247 hosting: web, business, WordPress, reseller, Windows and email hosting — with free SSL, backups, mailboxes, databases and 24/7 support.","body":"Hosting Compare CloudHost247 hosting: web, business, WordPress, reseller, Windows and email hosting — with free SSL, backups, mailboxes, databases and 24/7 support. Which hosting is which Choose a line Web Hosting Shared hosting for websites that need to be fast, secure and always up. Business Hosting More resources, stronger isolation and priority support handling for company sites. WordPress Hosting A WordPress-tuned runtime with caching, HTTPS and scheduled backups. Reseller Hosting Run your own hosting brand on infrastructure you do not have to operate. Windows Hosting ASP.NET, IIS and MSSQL for stacks that genuinely require Windows. Email Hosting Professional mailboxes on your own domain, with filtering and TLS. Plans currently configured on this deployment Live pricing The parts that are not add-ons Included with hosting SSL certificates Issued and renewed automatically for every domain on the account. Backups Scheduled jobs with a visible run history and a restore from your account. Databases MySQL-compatible databases alongside the site, managed in the same place. Migration An existing site and its mail moved across with a verified cutover. Security Isolation, platform patching, abuse filtering and monitored recovery. Control panels The panel families the platform is genuinely configured to provision. Why this page shows a catalogue instead of a price table"},
  {"href":"/hosting/web-hosting","title":"Web Hosting","category":"Page · Hosting","description":"CloudHost247 web hosting runs your website on managed infrastructure with SSD-backed storage, free SSL, mailboxes, databases and 24/7 support.","body":"Web Hosting CloudHost247 web hosting runs your website on managed infrastructure with SSD-backed storage, free SSL, mailboxes, databases and 24/7 support. A hosting account built for real websites What you get SSL as standard Every domain you add to the account can be issued a certificate, so browsers treat it as secure from the first visit. Mailboxes on your domain Create addresses at your own domain with spam filtering, and reach them from webmail or any mail client. Databases included MySQL-compatible databases for the applications you install, managed alongside the site rather than separately. Application installs Common applications can be installed onto your account, and managed from the same place as the rest of your services. Storage that is not fragile Web content lives on storage with scheduled backups, so a mistake is recoverable rather than final. Monitoring and alerts We watch the service so that an outage is something we are already responding to, not something you discover. From order to a live website Getting online Choose a plan Pick the hosting level that matches the site you are running today. Plans can be changed later without rebuilding the site. Point your domain Register a new domain with us or bring one you already own. We publish the DNS records and issue the certificate. Publish Upload the site, install an application, or build it with the CloudHost247 website builder — then manage it all from your account. Web hosting plans on this deployment Live pricing Migrations handled as a process, not a gamble Moving from another host"},
  {"href":"/hosting/business","title":"Business Hosting","category":"Page · Hosting","description":"Business hosting from CloudHost247 gives company sites more resources, stronger isolation, priority support and the headroom to run mail, apps and databases.","body":"Business Hosting Business hosting from CloudHost247 gives company sites more resources, stronger isolation, priority support and the headroom to run mail, apps and databases. Where business hosting differs Built for company workloads Headroom, not a ceiling Higher CPU, memory and process limits so a busy day does not turn into a 503 for your customers. Stronger isolation Business hosting is placed to reduce the blast radius of anything else on the platform, which matters when the site handles customer data. Priority support handling Business accounts are queued ahead of standard requests, reflecting what a business-hours outage actually costs. Business email alongside the site Company mailboxes live with the website, so a DNS change never silently breaks your email. Backups and recovery Scheduled backups with a restorable history, and a documented restore path rather than a promise. Monitored service Availability and resource use are watched by the platform so degradation is caught before it becomes an outage. Business hosting is usually the right answer when Who this fits The website is a revenue channel Enquiries, orders or bookings arrive through it, so an hour of downtime has a number attached. Mail runs on the same domain Staff mailboxes and the website need to stay in step when DNS or certificates change. Several applications share the account A CMS, a shop, a form handler and a CRM connector all need to coexist without starving each other. You need someone to answer quickly You want support handled as a priority rather than queued behind hobby accounts. Exact specifications are on the plan, not on this page Business hosting plans on this deployment Live pricing"},
  {"href":"/hosting/wordpress","title":"WordPress Hosting","category":"Page · Hosting","description":"WordPress hosting on CloudHost247: managed runtime, HTTPS, scheduled backups, database access and the operational work handled for you.","body":"WordPress Hosting WordPress hosting on CloudHost247: managed runtime, HTTPS, scheduled backups, database access and the operational work handled for you. Tuned for how WordPress actually behaves Why it is different Runtime tuned for WordPress PHP versions and limits chosen for WordPress rather than left at a generic default that produces white screens on plugin-heavy sites. Caching that survives updates Page caching that is invalidated properly when content changes, so the cache helps instead of showing visitors stale pages. HTTPS end to end A certificate on every domain and subdomain in the account, renewed automatically. Backups before you need them Scheduled backups of the site and its database, with restore handled from your account. Database access you can use Reach the WordPress database directly for exports, migrations or debugging — no support ticket needed. Hardened by default Platform-level filtering, sensible file permissions and abuse monitoring that runs whether or not you installed a plugin for it. Live in three moves Launching a WordPress site Install Install WordPress onto hosting that is already configured for it — no manual PHP configuration or database setup. Connect Point the domain and let the certificate issue, then configure permalinks, mail and your caching preferences. Maintain Run core, theme and plugin updates on your schedule, with a backup taken before you do. WordPress hosting plans on this deployment Live pricing Plugins are yours to choose — and yours to keep safe"},
  {"href":"/hosting/reseller","title":"Reseller Hosting","category":"Page · Hosting","description":"Reseller hosting from CloudHost247: separate accounts, your own branding, WHMCS-compatible billing and the infrastructure operated for you.","body":"Reseller Hosting Reseller hosting from CloudHost247: separate accounts, your own branding, WHMCS-compatible billing and the infrastructure operated for you. What you control, and what we take care of The reseller toolkit Customer accounts Create, suspend and remove client hosting accounts yourself, without waiting on a support queue. Your own nameservers Brand the DNS so clients see your infrastructure, not ours, in their domain settings. Your brand throughout The client experience carries your identity. The platform is meant to disappear behind your business. Billing platform compatible A WHMCS-compatible automation layer is supported, so orders and provisioning can be automated rather than handled by hand. Infrastructure you do not operate Hardware, network, patching and abuse handling are ours. Your obligation is your clients. Escalation path When something is genuinely infrastructure-level, there is a route to our engineers instead of a dead end. Reseller hosting plans on this deployment Live pricing What reseller hosting expects of you Before you start You support your own clients First-line support is yours. We handle the platform behind it. You own your commercial terms Your prices, your contracts, your refund policy — ours governs the account we sell you. You are accountable for content The Acceptable Use Policy applies to what your clients host, and enforcement reaches your account. You can grow a plan at a time Reseller allocations can be increased as your client base grows, without migrating them."},
  {"href":"/hosting/windows","title":"Windows Hosting","category":"Page · Hosting","description":"Windows hosting from CloudHost247 for ASP.NET and Windows-based stacks, with MSSQL databases, IIS configuration and managed certificates.","body":"Windows Hosting Windows hosting from CloudHost247 for ASP.NET and Windows-based stacks, with MSSQL databases, IIS configuration and managed certificates. A Windows stack that is actually maintained What it supports ASP.NET Run ASP.NET applications in the version the application targets, without rebuilding it for another platform. IIS management Bindings, application pools and site settings handled through a management interface rather than a ticket. MSSQL databases Microsoft SQL databases alongside the site, with the connection details you need for your configuration files. Certificates and HTTPS Certificates issued and renewed for each binding so secure endpoints do not expire silently. Backups Scheduled backups of site files and databases, restorable from your account. Monitoring The service is watched so failed application pools and exhausted disks are noticed before your users notice. Windows hosting plans on this deployment Live pricing Windows licensing is included, not passed to you"},
  {"href":"/hosting/email","title":"Email Hosting","category":"Page · Hosting","description":"Email hosting from CloudHost247: professional mailboxes on your domain with spam filtering, TLS, IMAP/POP/SMTP and webmail access.","body":"Email Hosting Email hosting from CloudHost247: professional mailboxes on your domain with spam filtering, TLS, IMAP/POP/SMTP and webmail access. What a business mailbox needs Mail that behaves Mailboxes on your domain Create, rename and remove addresses as your team changes, including aliases and forwarding. Filtering before delivery Spam and malware filtering applied ahead of the mailbox so your team is not the filter. TLS on the wire Encrypted connections for mail clients and webmail, so credentials and messages are not sent in the clear. SPF, DKIM and DMARC The DNS records that prove your mail is genuinely from your domain — published for you when DNS is managed here. Any mail client Standard IMAP, POP and SMTP, so Outlook, Apple Mail, Thunderbird and mobile clients all work. Deliverability watched Queue and delivery problems are monitored, because mail that silently stops arriving is the worst kind of outage. Email hosting plans on this deployment Live pricing Why authentication records matter Protect your domain's reputation"},
  {"href":"/hosting/developer","title":"Developer Hosting","category":"Page · Hosting","description":"Developer hosting from CloudHost247: check available runtimes, SSH, configuration and logs in the product catalogue. Git support depends on the selected panel.","body":"Developer Hosting Developer hosting from CloudHost247: check available runtimes, SSH, configuration and logs in the product catalogue. Git support depends on the selected panel. What you get to work with Developer surface Shell access SSH access is available on hosting products that include it; the selected plan and its access policy determine the scope. Deployment options The core platform deploys published application versions and configured images. Git-based source builds require an enabled control-panel integration. Environment configuration Set variables per application so configuration lives outside the code and can differ per environment. Logs you can read Application logs are available through the service interfaces that expose them; source-build output depends on the selected deployment integration. APIs for automation Authenticated APIs support selected service and deployment operations; consult the published API documentation for each endpoint. Telemetry Resource use and availability are recorded, so a regression is visible as a graph rather than a hunch. Pick the stack you already write Runtimes Node.js Long-running Node services with managed process supervision. PHP From a single script to a full framework, on a maintained runtime. Python WSGI and ASGI applications with virtual environments. Laravel Queues, scheduler, storage and deployment for Laravel apps. Docker Build and run container images with persistent volumes. APIs Host HTTP APIs with TLS, authentication and rate control. We will not pretend a runtime works before it does"},
  {"href":"/hosting/api","title":"API Hosting","category":"Page · Hosting","description":"Host HTTP APIs on CloudHost247 using an available runtime or container product; confirm TLS, network controls, logs and monitoring in the selected service catalogue.","body":"API Hosting Host HTTP APIs on CloudHost247 using an available runtime or container product; confirm TLS, network controls, logs and monitoring in the selected service catalogue. What we put around an API by default Non-negotiables TLS everywhere TLS is available on services and domains where the selected hosting product is configured to issue or accept certificates. Secrets outside the code Keys and connection strings are set as environment configuration per application, and are not returned once saved. Rate limiting Network and application rate controls depend on the selected product and its configured integrations; review the service details before designing around them. Real logs Request and error logs available on the deployment, so a 500 can be diagnosed without guesswork. Custom domains and certificates Attach the domain that belongs on the endpoint, including subdomains, with a certificate per hostname. Uptime and latency signals Monitoring coverage varies by service. The platform status and product pages identify the checks the current deployment can genuinely perform. Get an endpoint live Deployment Choose a deployment method The core deployment queue uses published application versions and configured images. Git source builds require a selected control-panel integration that explicitly supports them. Configure the environment Set the variables the API needs — database URL, signing keys, upstream credentials — as configuration on the application. Attach the domain Add the hostname, publish the DNS record and let the certificate issue. Then verify with a real request. Design your own authentication — we host it"},
  {"href":"/hosting/ssl","title":"SSL Certificates","category":"Page · Security","description":"Issue and renew SSL/TLS certificates for every domain you host with CloudHost247, with automated renewal, forced HTTPS and coverage for subdomains.","body":"SSL Certificates Issue and renew SSL/TLS certificates for every domain you host with CloudHost247, with automated renewal, forced HTTPS and coverage for subdomains. The failure modes we remove What is automated Issuance on demand Request a certificate for a hostname and it is validated and installed without you touching a CSR. Renewal before expiry Renewals run ahead of expiry, so the browser warning that costs you a customer never appears. Right hostnames, right coverage A certificate covers exactly the domains it is issued for — including www and subdomains where you need them. HTTPS enforced Optionally redirect all plain HTTP traffic, so a link that was written as http:// still lands on the encrypted site. Expiry visibility Every certificate in the account shows its status and expiry date, so nothing depends on someone remembering. Certificates per service Certificates attach at the service level, so a server, an application and a website each manage their own. SSL certificate plans on this deployment Live pricing Not every certificate type is offered, and we will say which"},
  {"href":"/hosting/backups","title":"Backups","category":"Page · Data","description":"Scheduled backups for CloudHost247 hosting, servers and applications, with visible job history and a documented restore path.","body":"Backups Scheduled backups for CloudHost247 hosting, servers and applications, with visible job history and a documented restore path. What the platform actually does How it works Scheduled, not manual Backup jobs run on a schedule you can see, so protection does not depend on someone remembering to click a button. What gets captured Files, databases and application data are captured according to the service, and each backup records what it contains. A job history Every run is recorded with its status and size, so a silently failing job is visible rather than assumed to be working. Restore from your account Restores are performed against the service they belong to, with the backup that will be used identified before it runs. Per-service scope Each hosting account, server and application has its own backup record, so restoring one thing does not touch another. Stored separately Backups are stored on storage separate from the live service, so losing the service does not lose the backup. What backups do not replace Say this out loud Your own copy of critical data For anything you cannot afford to lose, keep an export you control in addition to platform backups. A tested recovery plan Knowing what you will restore, in what order, is a decision backups cannot make for you. A version control system for code Backups return a service to a previous state. They are not a substitute for Git for your source code."},
  {"href":"/hosting/migration","title":"Website Migration","category":"Page · Hosting","description":"Move your website and email to CloudHost247 with a planned cutover: copy, verify on the new infrastructure, then switch DNS at your discretion.","body":"Website Migration Move your website and email to CloudHost247 with a planned cutover: copy, verify on the new infrastructure, then switch DNS at your discretion. Six steps, in this order The sequence Inventory We establish what is moving: files, databases, mailboxes, cron jobs, DNS records and any external service the site calls. Provision the target The destination account or server is created and configured to match the application's requirements before anything is copied. Copy the data Files and databases are transferred and the application is adjusted for the new path, hostname and connection details. Verify on a real hostname The copied site is served on a temporary hostname and checked: pages resolve, forms submit, mail authenticates, the certificate is valid. Switch DNS Only after verification, the domain's records are updated. Because the old host is untouched, this step is reversible. Confirm and tidy We confirm the live site and mail behave, then the old copies and any temporary hostnames are removed. What we need from you"},
  {"href":"/hosting/security","title":"Hosting Security","category":"Page · Security","description":"How CloudHost247 protects hosting: tenant isolation, platform patching, malware and abuse filtering, access control, certificates and monitored recovery.","body":"Hosting Security How CloudHost247 protects hosting: tenant isolation, platform patching, malware and abuse filtering, access control, certificates and monitored recovery. Where the protection actually sits Layers Isolation between tenants Accounts are separated at the service level so one compromised site is not a route into another customer's data. Platform patch management The operating systems, runtime versions and platform components we control are patched on a schedule, not when someone complains. Filtering before your site Known-malicious traffic patterns and abusive request rates are filtered at the platform edge, ahead of the application. Access control Account access uses strong credentials, session controls and multi-factor authentication, including passkeys. Encryption in transit TLS on every web endpoint and mail transport, with automated certificate renewal. Recovery and review Security-relevant events are logged, and the incident path is documented so a response does not start from zero. What is yours to own Shared responsibility Your application's code A vulnerable plugin or an injection flaw in your own code is not something the platform can patch for you. Your credentials Weak or reused passwords on accounts you control are the most common route in, on any platform. What you publish Content, scripts and third-party embeds you add to a site are your responsibility under the Acceptable Use Policy. Your data handling What personal data you collect, why, and for how long is your decision and your legal obligation."},
  {"href":"/platforms","title":"Platforms","category":"Page · Platform","description":"Published apps, managed databases, containers and deployment records on CloudHost247. Git source builds depend on a configured control-panel integration.","body":"Platforms Published apps, managed databases, containers and deployment records on CloudHost247. Git source builds depend on a configured control-panel integration. How much plumbing do you want to own? Choose your layer Application Marketplace Install a catalogue application with its dependencies configured for you. Application Hosting A managed environment around one application, with logs and backups. Databases MySQL, PostgreSQL, MariaDB, MongoDB and Redis as managed services. Containers & Docker Run a container image you built, with persistent volumes attached. PaaS Manage supported application deployments, environment settings and recorded outcomes; Git source builds depend on an enabled panel integration. Deployment Platform Track supported installs and updates with deployment status, step events and available recovery. A catalogue that reflects real deployments What is installed, not what is listed"},
  {"href":"/platforms/applications","title":"Application Hosting","category":"Page · Platform","description":"Managed application hosting from CloudHost247: an isolated environment per application, with logs, backups and configuration managed from your account.","body":"Application Hosting Managed application hosting from CloudHost247: an isolated environment per application, with logs, backups and configuration managed from your account. The pieces an application needs What you get Its own environment Dependencies and runtime for one application do not collide with another's, which removes an entire class of upgrade problem. Configuration Environment variables and settings are held per application, so the same image can run in more than one place with different values. Persistent volumes Data that must outlive a container or a rebuild is attached to a volume rather than left in the filesystem. Domain and certificate Attach a domain to the application and have a certificate issued for it. Logs Application output is captured per environment, so an error can be investigated where it happened. Backups Backup jobs can be scheduled against the application and its volumes. Install, configure, upgrade Lifecycle Install Choose the application from the marketplace. The platform provisions the resources the manifest declares. Configure Set the application's own settings, attach the domain, and connect any database it needs. Operate Watch it, back it up, and upgrade it when you decide to — not when the platform decides to."},
  {"href":"/platforms/databases","title":"Managed Databases","category":"Page · Data","description":"Managed database services on CloudHost247: MySQL-compatible, PostgreSQL, MariaDB, MongoDB and Redis, deployed with backups and access control.","body":"Managed Databases Managed database services on CloudHost247: MySQL-compatible, PostgreSQL, MariaDB, MongoDB and Redis, deployed with backups and access control. What the platform deploys Engines MySQL-compatible The default for most web applications and content management systems, and the engine most hosting features assume. MariaDB A MySQL-compatible engine where an application prefers or requires it. PostgreSQL For applications that want stricter SQL semantics, richer indexing or extensions. MongoDB Document storage for applications that model data as documents. Redis In-memory key-value storage for caching, sessions and queues. Backups Backup jobs scoped to the database service, so a restore brings back the data rather than the whole machine. Managed means operated — it does not mean clustered"},
  {"href":"/platforms/containers","title":"Containers & Docker","category":"Page · Platform","description":"Run containerised applications on CloudHost247 with Docker images, persistent volumes, environment configuration and per-application domains.","body":"Containers & Docker Run containerised applications on CloudHost247 with Docker images, persistent volumes, environment configuration and per-application domains. How it works in practice Containers here Images Deploy from an image reference the platform can pull, so the artefact you tested is the artefact that runs. Volumes State lives on volumes declared by the application, so replacing a container does not destroy its data. Environment configuration Configuration injected as environment variables, which is what makes one image runnable in several environments. Routing and TLS Attach a domain to the container and certificates are issued for it. Logs Container output captured per application, so debugging does not require shell access to a host. Resource visibility CPU, memory and traffic recorded, so a container that is quietly restarting becomes visible. What is not offered"},
  {"href":"/platforms/paas","title":"PaaS & Deployment Workflows","category":"Page · Platform","description":"Manage supported application deployments with recorded steps and per-app settings. Git source builds require an enabled control-panel integration.","body":"PaaS & Deployment Workflows Manage supported application deployments with recorded steps and per-app settings. Git source builds require an enabled control-panel integration. What the native deployment flow handles The platform layer Published application versions The marketplace exposes versions that have been published with a validated deployment manifest and configured image. Deployment records Installs and updates produce a durable record with status, step states and event history. Failure handling When an infrastructure step fails, the worker attempts to reverse completed steps and records whether recovery succeeded. Configuration per application Environment values and secrets are managed per installation, separately from the published application manifest. Routing Domains and certificates can be attached where the selected service and provider support them. Logs Deployment events and application logs are available through their respective service records; source-build output depends on a Git-enabled panel. Use the published deployment path Adopting it Select a published application Choose an application version the live catalogue makes available for deployment. Validate the target The platform checks the selected server, supported hosting type and capacity before it changes infrastructure. Provision the configured image The worker deploys the image and resources described by that application version’s manifest. Inspect the record Review status, step states, event history and any recovery result in the deployment record."},
  {"href":"/hosting/vps","title":"VPS Hosting","category":"Page · Cloud","description":"VPS hosting from CloudHost247: guaranteed virtual resources, full administrative access, a choice of operating system and live plan pricing from the catalogue.","body":"VPS Hosting VPS hosting from CloudHost247: guaranteed virtual resources, full administrative access, a choice of operating system and live plan pricing from the catalogue. VPS plans on this deployment Live pricing The difference between a VPS and a share of one What you get Guaranteed resources Your allocation of CPU, memory and storage is reserved for your server. A neighbour's traffic peak is not your performance problem. Administrator access Root or administrator access, so you install the runtime, the extensions and the services the application actually requires. Your choice of operating system Provision from the operating-system catalogue, and rebuild from a known-good image if a change goes wrong. Network control Firewall rules attached to the server, applied in a defined order, with the effective ruleset visible in your account. Backups Scheduled backup jobs against the server, with a run history and a restore performed from your account. Monitoring CPU, memory, storage and traffic recorded over time, so a capacity problem is a graph rather than a guess. A VPS expects you to operate it Choose carefully You own the operating system Root access means the patching, the hardening and the service configuration are yours. That is the trade you are making for control. Or hand it over Managed services cover the platform layer — patching, monitoring response and administration — without taking away your access. See managed services Not sure which size? Start from what the application needs: memory for its working set, cores for concurrency, storage for its data. Support will size it with you. Pick by what you need from the machine VPS, cloud or dedicated"},
  {"href":"/hosting/dedicated","title":"Dedicated Servers","category":"Page · Servers","description":"Dedicated servers from CloudHost247: an entire physical machine, full administrative control, hardware-level isolation and options for redundancy.","body":"Dedicated Servers Dedicated servers from CloudHost247: an entire physical machine, full administrative control, hardware-level isolation and options for redundancy. Dedicated configurations on this deployment Live pricing When a VPS is not the right answer Why physical Undivided performance Disk throughput, memory bandwidth and core count belong to your workload alone. That is what database and virtualisation hosts actually need. A physical boundary Isolation is a property of the hardware rather than of a hypervisor configuration, which is far easier to state in a compliance answer. Sized to the workload Configurations are chosen around measured requirements — cores, memory, storage and throughput — not a fixed tier list. Full control Administrator access to the whole machine: the operating system, the partitioning and every service on it. Managed if you want Patching, hardening, monitoring response and administration available as part of the service. Backups and recovery Backup jobs sized to the data, with a restore plan agreed before it is needed. Hardware detail is confirmed per configuration, not published as a guarantee"},
  {"href":"/hosting/cpanel","title":"cPanel Hosting","category":"Page · Hosting","description":"cPanel-based hosting from CloudHost247: mailboxes, databases, subdomains, SSL and one-click application installs, managed from the panel your team already knows.","body":"cPanel Hosting cPanel-based hosting from CloudHost247: mailboxes, databases, subdomains, SSL and one-click application installs, managed from the panel your team already knows. cPanel hosting plans on this deployment Live pricing Everything an account needs, in one place In the panel Mailboxes and forwarders Create addresses at your domain, set forwarders and autoresponders, and reach mail from webmail or a client. Databases MySQL-compatible databases with their own users, created and revoked from the panel. Domains and subdomains Add domains and subdomains to the account and manage their document roots. Certificates Issue and renew TLS for the domains in the account, with HTTPS enforced where you want it. Application installs Install common applications onto the account without setting up a database or a document root by hand. Backups Scheduled backups of the account with a run history and a restore from your CloudHost247 account. What panel you actually get is configuration, and the platform says which"},
  {"href":"/websites","title":"Websites","category":"Page · Websites","description":"Build a website on CloudHost247 with the website builder or the AI website builder, start from a template, launch a store, or have our designers do it for you.","body":"Websites Build a website on CloudHost247 with the website builder or the AI website builder, start from a template, launch a store, or have our designers do it for you. Build it yourself The builder Website Builder Pages, sections, media and publishing — with a real preview and a publish step, not a mock-up. AI Website Builder Write a description of the site you need and get real pages, copy and SEO to edit. Website Templates Start from a layout that is already structured for publishing instead of a blank page. Online Store Sell physical, digital and service products from the same platform that hosts the site. Or have it delivered Have it done for you Website Design Services Scoped, quoted and delivered by the CloudHost247 team — brief, design, build, handover. Hire an Expert Request a specialist for design, development, migration or ongoing maintenance. Website Migration Move an existing site onto CloudHost247 infrastructure with a verified cutover. Digital Marketing Campaigns, search visibility and a unified inbox for the enquiries the site produces. A website is not finished when it launches Run it properly HTTPS from the first visitor A certificate is issued for the domain you publish on, and renewed without anyone remembering to. SSL certificates Backups you can restore Scheduled backup jobs with a visible run history, so a mistake is recoverable. Backups Hosting that keeps up The site runs on hosting that can be upgraded without rebuilding the site. Web hosting A domain that belongs to you Register it with us or bring the one you own, and manage DNS from the same account. Domains"},
  {"href":"/help","title":"Help Center","category":"Page · Support","description":"CloudHost247 support: search the knowledge base and documentation, run a diagnostic tool, open a ticket with the team, or check what is happening right now.","body":"Help Center CloudHost247 support: search the knowledge base and documentation, run a diagnostic tool, open a ticket with the team, or check what is happening right now. Four routes to an answer Start here Documentation Platform references: APIs, deployment, environments, provisioning and operations. Diagnostic Tools Check DNS, propagation, IPs, headers and more — and see the result rather than a description of it. Knowledge Base Task-oriented guides for hosting, domains, email, servers and billing. Open a Ticket Reach the support team from your account, with your services already attached to the request. Four things that make a ticket solvable in one reply Before you open a ticket The service or domain involved A ticket opening with the affected service is already in the right queue. The subject line is what gets it there. What you expected and what happened Two sentences describing the difference resolves more tickets than any amount of log pasting. What changed just before A deployment, an update, a DNS change, a new plugin. Most incidents have a preceding change. Any error message, verbatim The exact text, copied rather than summarised. Paraphrased errors cost a round trip every time."},
  {"href":"/docs","title":"Documentation","category":"Page · Resources","description":"CloudHost247 platform documentation: API references, provisioning, deployment, domain services, billing, tools and operations guides.","body":"Documentation CloudHost247 platform documentation: API references, provisioning, deployment, domain services, billing, tools and operations guides. Guides in this repository Documentation index"},
  {"href":"/search","title":"Search","category":"Page · Utilities","description":"Search across CloudHost247 services, tools, documentation and policies.","body":"Search Search across CloudHost247 services, tools, documentation and policies. Find a service, tool or document Search"},
  {"href":"/status","title":"Service Status","category":"Page · Support","description":"Live service status for CloudHost247: the checks the platform can verify itself, reported honestly — including what is not monitored.","body":"Service Status Live service status for CloudHost247: the checks the platform can verify itself, reported honestly — including what is not monitored. Checks performed on page load Current state Why there is no historical uptime percentage"},
  {"href":"/offers","title":"Offers & Pricing","category":"Page · Marketing","description":"Current CloudHost247 pricing, rendered live from the configured product catalogue — plans, prices and billing cycles exactly as configured.","body":"Offers & Pricing Current CloudHost247 pricing, rendered live from the configured product catalogue — plans, prices and billing cycles exactly as configured. Products and plans currently configured Live catalogue No countdown timers, no invented discounts"},
  {"href":"/pricing","title":"Pricing","category":"Page · Marketing","description":"CloudHost247 pricing rendered from the live catalogue: hosting, cloud, domains and services at the prices actually configured.","body":"Pricing CloudHost247 pricing rendered from the live catalogue: hosting, cloud, domains and services at the prices actually configured. Configured products and plans Products"},
  {"href":"/security","title":"Security & Compliance","category":"Page · Company","description":"How CloudHost247 secures its platform and customer data: authentication, access control, encryption, isolation, logging and responsible disclosure.","body":"Security & Compliance How CloudHost247 secures its platform and customer data: authentication, access control, encryption, isolation, logging and responsible disclosure. What is implemented Controls Authentication Password hashing with a memory-hard algorithm, multi-factor authentication by TOTP, and passkey (WebAuthn) sign-in as a phishing-resistant option. Least privilege Role-based access for administrative functions, re-verified server-side on every request rather than trusted from the interface. Encryption TLS for every public endpoint and mail transport, with certificates issued and renewed automatically; sensitive values encrypted at rest. Isolation Customer services are separated, and provider credentials are held encrypted and used only by platform operations. Logging and audit Authentication events, administrative actions and infrastructure operations are recorded, giving an answer to who did what and when. Response A defined incident path: detection, containment, notification and review — documented before it is needed. If you find a vulnerability Disclosure Tell us, privately Report through the contact route with enough detail to reproduce it. Do not test against another customer's service or data. We will acknowledge and investigate Reports are triaged, and you get a response from a person who can act on it rather than an automated reply. Do not access data that is not yours Proof of concept that stops at the boundary of your own account is welcome. Going further is not authorised, whatever the intention. Certifications we do not claim"},
  {"href":"/about","title":"About CloudHost247","category":"Page · Company","description":"CloudHost247 Isc. builds and operates hosting, cloud, domain, application, website and developer platforms for businesses and developers worldwide.","body":"About CloudHost247 CloudHost247 Isc. builds and operates hosting, cloud, domain, application, website and developer platforms for businesses and developers worldwide. Principles we hold to How we work Say what is true No invented uptime figures, no certifications we do not hold, no data centre pins on a decorative map. Where something is not available, the product page says so. Show, do not imply Prices come from the catalogue, locations come from configuration, and a service status page reports only checks the platform can actually run. Operate what we sell Provisioning, monitoring, DNS, certificates, backups and reconciliation are platform features, not arrangements with somebody else. One relationship A domain problem, a server problem and a billing problem are the same support conversation rather than three vendors pointing at each other. Open about the seams Documentation describes what is finished and what is not, so nobody builds on a feature that exists only in a roadmap. Protect the boring things Strong credentials, encryption everywhere, least-privilege administration and logs that answer questions after the fact. What CloudHost247 covers The platform Domains Search, registration, transfer, DNS and the registrar toolkit. Hosting Web, business, WordPress, reseller and Windows hosting. Cloud & servers VPS, cloud, dedicated and enterprise servers with operations. Platforms Applications, databases, containers and PaaS. Developers Runtimes, Git deployment, environments and APIs. Websites Builder, AI builder, stores and design services. Tools DNS, IP, network, security, developer and webmaster tools. Support Documentation, diagnostics, knowledge base and tickets. CloudHost247 Isc."},
  {"href":"/blog","title":"News & Updates","category":"Page · Company","description":"Platform releases and product notes from CloudHost247 — what shipped, what it replaces, and what it deliberately does not do yet.","body":"News & Updates Platform releases and product notes from CloudHost247 — what shipped, what it replaces, and what it deliberately does not do yet. Platform releases Release notes"},
  {"href":"/docs/api-catalog","title":"Catalog API","category":"Documentation · APIs","description":"This document is the API contract for the catalog/application-façade layer added in Phase 3. It covers everything under /api/v1/catalog/ (public) and /api/v1/admin/catalog/ (authenticated admin). Keep","body":"Catalog API This document is the API contract for the catalog/application-façade layer added in Phase 3. It covers everything under /api/v1/catalog/ (public) and /api/v1/admin/catalog/ (authenticated admin). Keep"},
  {"href":"/docs/api-commerce","title":"Commerce API","category":"Documentation · APIs","description":"This document is the API contract for Phase 5A, \"Commerce foundation\": a customer's cart and the orders it becomes when checked out. Keep this in sync with the code - the source of truth is cloudhost2","body":"Commerce API This document is the API contract for Phase 5A, \"Commerce foundation\": a customer's cart and the orders it becomes when checked out. Keep this in sync with the code - the source of truth is cloudhost2"},
  {"href":"/docs/api-billing","title":"Billing API","category":"Documentation · APIs","description":"This document is the API contract for Phase 5B, \"Billing foundation\": real invoices, issued automatically and atomically when an order is checked out (Phase 5A), and the append-only billing ledger beh","body":"Billing API This document is the API contract for Phase 5B, \"Billing foundation\": real invoices, issued automatically and atomically when an order is checked out (Phase 5A), and the append-only billing ledger beh"},
  {"href":"/docs/api-payments","title":"Payments API","category":"Documentation · APIs","description":"This document is the API contract for Phase 5C, \"Payment integration\": a payment gateway abstraction, a manual/offline (bank-transfer) gateway with staff-confirmed resolution, and a self-contained san","body":"Payments API This document is the API contract for Phase 5C, \"Payment integration\": a payment gateway abstraction, a manual/offline (bank-transfer) gateway with staff-confirmed resolution, and a self-contained san"},
  {"href":"/docs/api-customer-app","title":"Customer application API","category":"Documentation · APIs","description":"This document is the API contract for the Phase 4 \"Customer App\" layer: self-service customer account management, passive/informational service and domain records, and a basic support ticket system, p","body":"Customer application API This document is the API contract for the Phase 4 \"Customer App\" layer: self-service customer account management, passive/informational service and domain records, and a basic support ticket system, p"},
  {"href":"/docs/domain-services-architecture","title":"Domain services architecture","category":"Documentation · Services","description":"This document records the Phase 1 audit and data/provider architecture for the Domain Services platform. It deliberately does not present a search box, price, availability, registration, transfer, auc","body":"Domain services architecture This document records the Phase 1 audit and data/provider architecture for the Domain Services platform. It deliberately does not present a search box, price, availability, registration, transfer, auc"},
  {"href":"/docs/domain-brokerage","title":"Domain brokerage","category":"Documentation · Services","description":"The Node platform's Domain Brokerage Engine is provider-neutral. src/domain-brokerage/provider.ts defines the adapter contract and capability registry; database provider rows are not considered connec","body":"Domain brokerage The Node platform's Domain Brokerage Engine is provider-neutral. src/domain-brokerage/provider.ts defines the adapter contract and capability registry; database provider rows are not considered connec"},
  {"href":"/docs/server-provisioning","title":"Server provisioning","category":"Documentation · Services","description":"CloudHost247 keeps the customer-facing operating-system catalog separate from provider image identifiers:","body":"Server provisioning CloudHost247 keeps the customer-facing operating-system catalog separate from provider image identifiers:"},
  {"href":"/docs/server-agent","title":"Server agent","category":"Documentation · Services","description":"The agent source lives in /server-agent/ (its own package, zero npm dependencies, Node ≥ 20). See /server-agent/README.md for install instructions and the request-authentication spec. This document is","body":"Server agent The agent source lives in /server-agent/ (its own package, zero npm dependencies, Node ≥ 20). See /server-agent/README.md for install instructions and the request-authentication spec. This document is"},
  {"href":"/docs/platform-services-architecture","title":"Platform services architecture","category":"Documentation · Services","description":"The CLOUDHOST247 platform (the Node/TypeScript application in cloudhost247-node/) runs the domain, hosting, website-building, AI-website, store, expert, marketing, logo, inbox and commerce services. T","body":"Platform services architecture The CLOUDHOST247 platform (the Node/TypeScript application in cloudhost247-node/) runs the domain, hosting, website-building, AI-website, store, expert, marketing, logo, inbox and commerce services. T"},
  {"href":"/docs/vps-deployment","title":"VPS deployment (Ubuntu 24.04)","category":"Documentation · Operations","description":"Target: a plain Linux VPS running Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (noble) with root access. This is the only supported deployment target. The cPanel/Passenger path was retired on 2026-11-15 (see Appendix B).","body":"VPS deployment (Ubuntu 24.04) Target: a plain Linux VPS running Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (noble) with root access. This is the only supported deployment target. The cPanel/Passenger path was retired on 2026-11-15 (see Appendix B)."},
  {"href":"/docs/passkey","title":"Passkeys and WebAuthn","category":"Documentation · Accounts","description":"Reference documentation for modules/addons/cloudhost247_passkey. The README in that module covers installation and day-to-day operation; this document covers the security decisions, the threat model a","body":"Passkeys and WebAuthn Reference documentation for modules/addons/cloudhost247_passkey. The README in that module covers installation and day-to-day operation; this document covers the security decisions, the threat model a"},
  {"href":"/docs/mrz-developer-tool","title":"Document tools (MRZ)","category":"Documentation · Accounts","description":"The CloudHost247 ePassport Machine Readable Zone (MRZ) Developer Tool provides a native, privacy-first utility for:","body":"Document tools (MRZ) The CloudHost247 ePassport Machine Readable Zone (MRZ) Developer Tool provides a native, privacy-first utility for:"},
  {"href":"/docs/integrations-google-ads","title":"Google Ads integration","category":"Documentation · Operations","description":"CloudHost247 provides an optional browser-side Google Ads tag integration managed from Admin → Google Ads conversions (/admin/integrations/google-ads). It uses the existing marketing integration store","body":"Google Ads integration CloudHost247 provides an optional browser-side Google Ads tag integration managed from Admin → Google Ads conversions (/admin/integrations/google-ads). It uses the existing marketing integration store"},
  {"href":"/tools/dns/propagation","title":"DNS Propagation Checker","category":"Tool","description":"Query the same record against multiple public resolvers worldwide.","body":"DNS Propagation Checker Query the same record against multiple public resolvers worldwide. Sends the same DNS question to each enabled resolver in the CloudHost247 resolver registry and reports, per resolver, the answer, response time and status. Results describe exactly the resolvers queried — CloudHost247 does not claim that these answers represent global propagation."},
  {"href":"/tools/dns/lookup","title":"DNS Lookup","category":"Tool","description":"Look up A, AAAA, CNAME, MX, NS, TXT, SOA, SRV, CAA, PTR, DS and DNSKEY records.","body":"DNS Lookup Look up A, AAAA, CNAME, MX, NS, TXT, SOA, SRV, CAA, PTR, DS and DNSKEY records. Queries a selected CloudHost247 resolver for one record type and shows every answer with TTL, priority (MX/SRV) and the resolver that answered. DS and DNSKEY come from the DNSSEC zone."},
  {"href":"/tools/dns/health","title":"DNS Health Checker","category":"Tool","description":"Run every DNS, delegation, email-authentication and DNSSEC check for a domain.","body":"DNS Health Checker Run every DNS, delegation, email-authentication and DNSSEC check for a domain. Runs a battery of independent checks against the domain's authoritative servers and public resolvers: NS delegation consistency, A/AAAA/CNAME, MX, SPF, DKIM, DMARC, BIMI, CAA, SOA, TTL consistency, DNSSEC and resolution failures. Each check reports PASS, WARNING, ERROR, NOT_CHECKED or UNKNOWN with its own explanation."},
  {"href":"/tools/dns/mx","title":"MX Lookup","category":"Tool","description":"Resolve MX hosts, their addresses, reverse DNS and mail provider.","body":"MX Lookup Resolve MX hosts, their addresses, reverse DNS and mail provider. Resolves the domain's MX records, then resolves each mail host to IPv4/IPv6 and performs a reverse lookup. The provider is identified only when the MX hostname matches a known CloudHost247 mapping; otherwise it is reported as Unknown rather than guessed."},
  {"href":"/tools/dns/spf","title":"SPF Checker","category":"Tool","description":"Parse and validate the domain's SPF policy, including DNS lookup count.","body":"SPF Checker Parse and validate the domain's SPF policy, including DNS lookup count. Fetches the SPF TXT record, parses every mechanism and modifier, checks the RFC 7208 syntax, counts the DNS lookups the record requires (limit 10) and flags common misconfigurations: multiple SPF records, deprecated ptr, missing terminal all, lookups beyond 10, and include loops."},
  {"href":"/tools/dns/dmarc","title":"DMARC Checker","category":"Tool","description":"Inspect and validate a _dmarc policy, tag by tag.","body":"DMARC Checker Inspect and validate a _dmarc policy, tag by tag. Fetches _dmarc.<domain and validates every tag (v, p, sp, pct, rua, ruf, adkim, aspf, fo, rf, ri), explains what the policy means for receiving mail servers, and warns about combinations that are syntactically valid but operationally risky."},
  {"href":"/tools/dns/dmarc-generator","title":"DMARC Record Generator","category":"Tool","description":"Build a correctly formatted _dmarc record interactively.","body":"DMARC Record Generator Build a correctly formatted _dmarc record interactively. Generates the TXT value for a _dmarc record from a guided form and shows exactly where to publish it. Generation is deterministic and validated server-side, so the value can be pasted into CloudHost247 DNS management, cPanel or any DNS host."},
  {"href":"/tools/dns/dkim","title":"DKIM Checker","category":"Tool","description":"Check selector._domainkey records for one or more selectors.","body":"DKIM Checker Check selector._domainkey records for one or more selectors. Queries the DKIM public-key records for the selectors you supply, parses the key, reports the key type and flags syntax problems. CloudHost247 cannot confirm a signature actually validates from the public key alone — when an external DKIM verifier provider is configured, that extra verification is offered explicitly."},
  {"href":"/tools/dns/bimi","title":"BIMI Checker","category":"Tool","description":"Inspect the BIMI record, logo URL and VMC certificate URL.","body":"BIMI Checker Inspect the BIMI record, logo URL and VMC certificate URL. Fetches default._bimi.<domain, parses the l= and a= tags, validates the URL shape, and reports whether the DMARC policy satisfies BIMI's enforcement prerequisite. It reports what the DNS says; it does not claim a mailbox provider will display the logo."},
  {"href":"/tools/dns/dnskey","title":"DNSKEY Lookup","category":"Tool","description":"Show the zone's DNSKEY records with key tag, algorithm, flags and public key.","body":"DNSKEY Lookup Show the zone's DNSKEY records with key tag, algorithm, flags and public key. Queries DNSKEY at the zone apex, computes the RFC 4034 §5.1.4 key tag for each key and reports SEP/Zone flags, protocol and algorithm. Presence of DNSKEY records does not by itself prove DNSSEC validation; the DNS Health Checker reports delegation evidence separately."},
  {"href":"/tools/dns/ds","title":"DS Lookup","category":"Tool","description":"Show the DS records published by the parent zone and the DNSSEC chain state.","body":"DS Lookup Show the DS records published by the parent zone and the DNSSEC chain state. Queries DS at the parent zone (or at the zone itself when it is a TLD), lists key tag, algorithm, digest type and digest, and reports whether a matching DNSKEY exists at the child so the delegation chain can be described factually."},
  {"href":"/tools/dns/reverse","title":"Reverse DNS / PTR Lookup","category":"Tool","description":"PTR lookup for IPv4/IPv6 with forward-confirmed reverse DNS.","body":"Reverse DNS / PTR Lookup PTR lookup for IPv4/IPv6 with forward-confirmed reverse DNS. Builds the in-addr.arpa / ip6.arpa name, resolves its PTR records and then resolves each returned hostname forward to confirm the address appears in its A/AAAA records (forward-confirmed reverse DNS)."},
  {"href":"/tools/dns/reverse-ip","title":"Reverse IP Lookup","category":"Tool","description":"Find hostnames hosted on an IP address, when a data provider is configured.","body":"Reverse IP Lookup Find hostnames hosted on an IP address, when a data provider is configured. There is no public DNS mechanism that lists the domains behind an IP address. This tool therefore requires an administrator-configured reverse-IP data provider and returns CONFIGURATION_REQUIRED until one exists. It never claims to discover every domain on an address."},
  {"href":"/tools/ip/lookup","title":"IP Address Lookup","category":"Tool","description":"ASN, organisation, country, reverse DNS and network range for an IP.","body":"IP Address Lookup ASN, organisation, country, reverse DNS and network range for an IP. Combines the free, keyless Team Cymru DNS origin lookup (ASN, prefix, registry, country) with reverse DNS and, when a geolocation provider is configured, city/region/timezone enrichment. Address version, class (public/private/reserved) and prefix are always reported."},
  {"href":"/tools/ip/my-ip","title":"What Is My IP","category":"Tool","description":"Show the public IP verified for this connection, or say plainly why none is claimed.","body":"What Is My IP Show the public IP verified for this connection, or say plainly why none is claimed. Reports the address CloudHost247's configured network boundary verified for your request (and the IPv6 address separately when the connection used IPv6), or states the reason nothing is claimed when it cannot verify one — a forwarding header is never substituted for a verified address. Adds user-agent and, when detectable, the negotiated TLS protocol/cipher, and the non-credential headers your browser sent. No attempt is made to fingerprint the device beyond what the browser sends."},
  {"href":"/tools/ip/whois","title":"IP WHOIS","category":"Tool","description":"Registry data for an IPv4/IPv6 address over RDAP.","body":"IP WHOIS Registry data for an IPv4/IPv6 address over RDAP. Queries RDAP (the structured, standards-based successor to port-43 WHOIS) for the address: network handle, name, range, CIDR blocks, registrant organisation, abuse contact, events and remarks. The RDAP bootstrap endpoint is operator-configurable."},
  {"href":"/tools/ip/domain-to-ip","title":"Domain → IP","category":"Tool","description":"Resolve a hostname to IPv4/IPv6 with the full CNAME chain.","body":"Domain → IP Resolve a hostname to IPv4/IPv6 with the full CNAME chain. Resolves A and AAAA through a chosen CloudHost247 resolver, showing the CNAME chain, TTLs and response time for each answer."},
  {"href":"/tools/ip/ip-to-hostname","title":"IP → Hostname","category":"Tool","description":"Reverse DNS for an address, with FCRDNS confirmation.","body":"IP → Hostname Reverse DNS for an address, with FCRDNS confirmation. Performs the PTR lookup for an address and confirms each hostname resolves back to it."},
  {"href":"/tools/ip/isp","title":"ISP Lookup","category":"Tool","description":"Network operator, ASN and country for an IP address.","body":"ISP Lookup Network operator, ASN and country for an IP address. Uses the keyless Team Cymru DNS origin service for ASN/prefix/registry/country and the reverse-DNS operator name, and adds ISP/carrier names from a geolocation provider when one is configured."},
  {"href":"/tools/ip/converters","title":"IP Converters","category":"Tool","description":"Decimal ↔ IP, IPv4 ↔ IPv6, IPv6 compression/expansion, CIDR ↔ range.","body":"IP Converters Decimal ↔ IP, IPv4 ↔ IPv6, IPv6 compression/expansion, CIDR ↔ range. Deterministic conversions with the intermediate steps shown: IPv4/IPv6 to decimal and back, IPv4-mapped IPv6 and NAT64 forms, IPv6 compression and expansion, and IPv6 CIDR ↔ address range."},
  {"href":"/tools/network/subnet-calculator","title":"Subnet Calculator","category":"Tool","description":"IPv4/IPv6 network, broadcast, host range, masks and splitting.","body":"Subnet Calculator IPv4/IPv6 network, broadcast, host range, masks and splitting. Computes network address, broadcast, first/last usable host, address count, CIDR notation, subnet mask, wildcard mask and binary forms for IPv4 and IPv6, and can split a network into equal subnets."},
  {"href":"/tools/network/ping","title":"Ping Tool","category":"Tool","description":"Measure reachability and latency from the CloudHost247 server.","body":"Ping Tool Measure reachability and latency from the CloudHost247 server. Uses the ICMP ping utility when the deployment allows it, and otherwise falls back to TCP connect timing against the port you choose — clearly labelled as TCP latency, never presented as ICMP. Targets are validated, private ranges are refused and results are rate limited."},
  {"href":"/tools/network/traceroute","title":"Traceroute","category":"Tool","description":"Hop-by-hop path to a target, where the environment permits.","body":"Traceroute Hop-by-hop path to a target, where the environment permits. Runs the system traceroute utility with a bounded hop count and timeout when the binary exists and the environment allows it. When it does not, the tool reports UNAVAILABLE_IN_THIS_ENVIRONMENT and explains why rather than returning fabricated hops."},
  {"href":"/tools/network/port-checker","title":"Port Checker","category":"Tool","description":"Check whether a TCP port on a public host accepts connections.","body":"Port Checker Check whether a TCP port on a public host accepts connections. Opens a TCP connection to a validated public host and port with a short timeout, reporting open, closed, filtered/timeout or unreachable. Single ports and short ranges only, with strict per-account limits; private and reserved address ranges are refused."},
  {"href":"/tools/network/mac-lookup","title":"MAC Address Lookup","category":"Tool","description":"Inspect MAC address bits and query a configured IEEE OUI reference.","body":"MAC Address Lookup Inspect MAC address bits and query a configured IEEE OUI reference. Inspects unicast/multicast and global/local bits. Vendor information comes from a configured IEEE OUI source, cached with its load time; unavailable source data is explicitly reported, never invented."},
  {"href":"/tools/network/mac-generator","title":"MAC Address Generator","category":"Tool","description":"Generate valid random, locally-administered or globally-administered MACs.","body":"MAC Address Generator Generate valid random, locally-administered or globally-administered MACs. Generates cryptographically random MAC addresses with the correct unicast/multicast and U/L bits for the requested mode."},
  {"href":"/tools/network/asn","title":"ASN WHOIS","category":"Tool","description":"Autonomous system details, announced prefixes and registry.","body":"ASN WHOIS Autonomous system details, announced prefixes and registry. Queries RDAP for the AS number and the DNS-based Team Cymru origin service for announced prefixes, then resolves the AS name from RDAP. Results are attributable: every field lists the source that produced it."},
  {"href":"/tools/network/speed-test","title":"Internet Speed Test","category":"Tool","description":"Browser-based download, upload and latency measurement with hard limits.","body":"Internet Speed Test Browser-based download, upload and latency measurement with hard limits. Measures throughput between your browser and CloudHost247 using bounded transfers: the server caps each measurement by size and duration, and rate limits each client. Latency is measured with small request/response timing and jitter is reported when at least three samples are collected."},
  {"href":"/tools/developer/http-headers","title":"HTTP Headers Checker","category":"Tool","description":"Status, headers, redirect chain, cache and security-header analysis.","body":"HTTP Headers Checker Status, headers, redirect chain, cache and security-header analysis. Fetches a URL through the SSRF-protected client, follows redirects with a hop limit, and reports the status code, every response header, the redirect chain, and an assessment of security headers (HSTS, CSP, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options/frame-ancestors, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy) and cache directives."},
  {"href":"/tools/developer/server-os","title":"Website OS Checker","category":"Tool","description":"Infer server software with an explicit confidence level.","body":"Website OS Checker Infer server software with an explicit confidence level. Reads Server, X-Powered-By, Via and proxy-identifying headers and reports each technology with a confidence level — Confirmed when the server states it, Likely when derived from several weak signals, Unknown when nothing reliable is present. No probing of the server beyond the single HTTP request."},
  {"href":"/tools/developer/smtp-test","title":"SMTP Tester","category":"Tool","description":"Test an SMTP server's reachability, TLS and (optionally) authentication.","body":"SMTP Tester Test an SMTP server's reachability, TLS and (optionally) authentication. Connects to the SMTP host, reads the banner, negotiates STARTTLS or implicit TLS, and reports the server capabilities, certificate summary and whether AUTH is offered. When you supply credentials they are used for that single test only: never logged, never stored, and never echoed back."},
  {"href":"/tools/developer/email-header","title":"Email Header Analyzer","category":"Tool","description":"Parse a raw message header: Received chain, auth results, sending IP.","body":"Email Header Analyzer Parse a raw message header: Received chain, auth results, sending IP. Parses a pasted header, reconstructs the Received chain with per-hop delays, extracts SPF/DKIM/DMARC results from Authentication-Results, identifies the sending IP and mail servers, and flags alignment mismatches between From, Return-Path and the authenticated domain."},
  {"href":"/tools/developer/json","title":"JSON Tools","category":"Tool","description":"Viewer, formatter, beautifier, minifier and validator.","body":"JSON Tools Viewer, formatter, beautifier, minifier and validator. Validates JSON with precise error positions, formats it with the indentation you choose, minifies it, and can sort keys. All processing happens in the browser; the API endpoint exists so the same behaviour is available to integrations and is covered by tests."},
  {"href":"/tools/developer/encoding","title":"Encoding Tools","category":"Tool","description":"Base64, MD5, binary ↔ text, ROT13 and Morse code.","body":"Encoding Tools Base64, MD5, binary ↔ text, ROT13 and Morse code. Encodes and decodes Base64 (UTF-8 safe), computes MD5, converts between text and binary, applies ROT13 and translates to/from Morse code. MD5 is provided for checksum/interoperability work only and the UI states plainly that it is unsuitable for password storage."},
  {"href":"/tools/developer/url","title":"URL Tools","category":"Tool","description":"Multi-URL opener, rewrite-rule and .htaccess generators.","body":"URL Tools Multi-URL opener, rewrite-rule and .htaccess generators. Opens several URLs in browser tabs (client-side only — no server-side fetching merely to open a link), parses and explains URL components, and generates common Apache rewrite/redirect rules and .htaccess blocks with safe defaults."},
  {"href":"/tools/developer/user-agent","title":"User Agent Tool","category":"Tool","description":"Show the user-agent and headers your browser actually sent.","body":"User Agent Tool Show the user-agent and headers your browser actually sent. Displays the exact User-Agent string and request headers CloudHost247 received, so a support conversation can start from the same facts."},
  {"href":"/tools/webmaster/broken-links","title":"Broken Link Checker","category":"Tool","description":"Crawl a site within strict limits and report failing links.","body":"Broken Link Checker Crawl a site within strict limits and report failing links. Crawls the same host starting from the URL you provide, within hard limits on pages, links, runtime and response size, and reports each link with its status, type (internal/external), redirect chain, error and the page it was found on. Private and reserved destinations are refused."},
  {"href":"/tools/webmaster/open-graph","title":"Open Graph Checker","category":"Tool","description":"Inspect og: and Twitter card metadata and preview the link.","body":"Open Graph Checker Inspect og: and Twitter card metadata and preview the link. Parses Open Graph and Twitter/X card tags, warns about missing or malformed required properties, resolves relative image URLs and renders a preview of how the link is likely to appear."},
  {"href":"/tools/webmaster/robots-generator","title":"robots.txt Generator","category":"Tool","description":"Build a valid robots.txt with sitemaps and crawl delay.","body":"robots.txt Generator Build a valid robots.txt with sitemaps and crawl delay. Generates robots.txt from a guided form (user-agent groups, allow/disallow rules, sitemaps, crawl-delay, common presets), validating directives so the file cannot be emitted in a malformed state."},
  {"href":"/tools/webmaster/serp-simulator","title":"SERP Simulator","category":"Tool","description":"Preview a search result snippet for title, URL and description length.","body":"SERP Simulator Preview a search result snippet for title, URL and description length. Renders a desktop and mobile search-result preview and reports pixel-width and character guidance for the title and description. It is explicitly a simulator for appearance only; it shows no ranking data."},
  {"href":"/tools/security/ssl","title":"SSL Certificate Checker","category":"Tool","description":"Certificate chain, validity, SANs, protocol and expiry for a host.","body":"SSL Certificate Checker Certificate chain, validity, SANs, protocol and expiry for a host. Opens a real TLS connection, reports the leaf and chain certificates (subject, issuer, SANs, validity, signature algorithm, key parameters), the negotiated protocol and cipher, hostname match, and days remaining. Private keys are never requested or displayed."},
  {"href":"/tools/security/ip-blacklist","title":"IP Blacklist Checker","category":"Tool","description":"Check an IP against the DNS blocklists the operator has enabled.","body":"IP Blacklist Checker Check an IP against the DNS blocklists the operator has enabled. Queries each enabled DNS-based blocklist for the address and reports listed / not listed / error per provider, with the listing code or text the provider returned and delisting guidance. Providers are managed by a Super Admin — nothing is hard-coded."},
  {"href":"/tools/security/password","title":"Password Tools","category":"Tool","description":"Generate strong passwords and evaluate strength locally.","body":"Password Tools Generate strong passwords and evaluate strength locally. Generates random passwords with the character classes and length you choose, evaluates the strength of a password using client-side entropy estimation against common patterns, and explains the difference between a one-way password hash and reversible encryption."},
  {"href":"/tools/security/bin-checker","title":"BIN Checker","category":"Tool","description":"Issuer information for a card BIN/IIN from a configured provider.","body":"BIN Checker Issuer information for a card BIN/IIN from a configured provider. Accepts only the first 6–8 digits (the BIN/IIN) and returns the issuer data the configured provider supplies. CloudHost247 never accepts, transmits or stores a full card number, and this is not a card-validation or testing service."},
  {"href":"/tools/business-tools","title":"Business Tools","category":"Tool","description":"Twenty-one payroll, tax, document and provider-comparison tools that run entirely in your browser.","body":"Business Tools Twenty-one payroll, tax, document and provider-comparison tools that run entirely in your browser. The Business Tools directory: 5 calculators (PAYE and net salary under the Nigeria Tax Act 2025, PenCom pension, VAT at 7.5%, total employer cost, and Earned Wage Access ROI), 12 generators (job descriptions, offer letters, payslips, NDAs, employment contracts, CVs, invoices, business cards, employee identifiers, ID badges, organization charts and LinkedIn comment drafts) and 4 comparisons (accounting systems, expense platforms, NHIA-accredited HMOs and PenCom-licensed PFAs). Every calculation runs client-side: salary figures, employee names, contract terms and client details are never uploaded, logged or stored. Each tool that applies a statutory rate names its jurisdiction, source and effective date, and each planning estimate is labelled as one. These tools produce figures and drafts for you to check — they are not tax, legal or financial advice."},
  {"href":"/tools/mrz-generator","title":"MRZ Generator","category":"Tool","description":"Generate, validate and parse ICAO Doc 9303 machine-readable zones, with per-layout field-width and check-digit validation.","body":"MRZ Generator Generate, validate and parse ICAO Doc 9303 machine-readable zones, with per-layout field-width and check-digit validation. Builds ICAO Doc 9303 machine-readable zones from the document fields you enter, validates the structure and the 7-3-1 check digits of an existing zone, and parses a supplied zone back into labelled fields. The page states which layout it is producing and enforces that layout\\u2019s field widths: a value that cannot fit is rejected with a message naming the field and its limit rather than being truncated. Names are transliterated to the ICAO Latin character set and an unsupported character is reported instead of being silently removed. Validation is syntactic — structure, widths, character set and check digits — and a zone that passes it is still not evidence that a physical or electronic document is genuine. Generation and validation run in your browser; the documented API path exists for integration testing and never caches, logs or persists the values you submit. This tool works on machine-readable text only and does not produce passport artwork."},
  {"href":"/tools/domain/punycode","title":"Punycode / IDN Converter","category":"Tool","description":"Convert between Unicode domain names and their ASCII (punycode) form.","body":"Punycode / IDN Converter Convert between Unicode domain names and their ASCII (punycode) form. Uses standards-compliant IDNA processing (Node's URL hostname parser, which implements UTS46-style mapping) to convert between a Unicode domain and its punycode form, validating the result and reporting the label-by-label conversion."},
  {"href":"/tools/domain/search","title":"Domain Availability","category":"Tool","description":"Check whether a domain is available, using CloudHost247's registrar integration.","body":"Domain Availability Check whether a domain is available, using CloudHost247's registrar integration. Uses the existing CloudHost247 Domain Services providers (registrar APIs and RDAP) to check availability, and returns the same states the domain search does: available, registered, premium, unsupported, unknown. Signed-in customers can add a result straight to the cart."},
  {"href":"/tools/productivity/word-counter","title":"Word & Text Counter","category":"Tool","description":"Words, characters, sentences, paragraphs and reading time.","body":"Word & Text Counter Words, characters, sentences, paragraphs and reading time. Counts words, characters (with and without spaces), sentences and paragraphs, and estimates reading time from word count."},
  {"href":"/tools/productivity/lorem-ipsum","title":"Lorem Ipsum Generator","category":"Tool","description":"Generate placeholder text by words, sentences or paragraphs.","body":"Lorem Ipsum Generator Generate placeholder text by words, sentences or paragraphs. Generates classical Lorem Ipsum placeholder text in the quantity you request, with a choice of starting with \"Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet…\"."},
  {"href":"/tools/productivity/notepad","title":"Online Notepad","category":"Tool","description":"A scratch pad that stays in your browser.","body":"Online Notepad A scratch pad that stays in your browser. A distraction-free text area with local persistence in your browser only. Nothing typed into the notepad is sent to CloudHost247 unless you explicitly save it as a report."},
  {"href":"/tools/productivity/small-text","title":"Small Text Generator","category":"Tool","description":"Convert text to small caps, superscript and subscript Unicode.","body":"Small Text Generator Convert text to small caps, superscript and subscript Unicode. Maps letters to Unicode small-cap, superscript and subscript equivalents. Characters without a mapping are left unchanged and reported, so the output never silently loses content."},
  {"href":"/tools/productivity/invisible-character","title":"Invisible Character Generator","category":"Tool","description":"Copy zero-width and invisible Unicode characters.","body":"Invisible Character Generator Copy zero-width and invisible Unicode characters. Provides the standard invisible Unicode characters with their code points and names, ready to copy. Each entry is labelled with its code point so the output is auditable."},
  {"href":"/tools/productivity/runic","title":"Runic Translator","category":"Tool","description":"Transliterate Latin text to Elder Futhark runes and back.","body":"Runic Translator Transliterate Latin text to Elder Futhark runes and back. Transliterates Latin letters to Elder Futhark runes using a documented, deterministic mapping (digraphs first), and transliterates back. Characters with no runic equivalent are reported rather than dropped."},
  {"href":"/tools/productivity/qr","title":"QR Code Generator","category":"Tool","description":"Create QR codes for URLs, text, email, phone, WiFi and vCards.","body":"QR Code Generator Create QR codes for URLs, text, email, phone, WiFi and vCards. Generates QR codes server-side (so the same PNG/SVG is reproducible from the API) for URLs, plain text, email, phone numbers, WiFi credentials and vCards. Nothing you enter is stored; the response contains the image and nothing else."},
  {"href":"/tools/productivity/qr-scanner","title":"QR Scanner","category":"Tool","description":"Scan a QR code from your camera or an image file.","body":"QR Scanner Scan a QR code from your camera or an image file. Decodes QR codes in the browser using the device camera or an uploaded image, using the platform's QR reader support. Decoded content is shown for review and is never uploaded unless you explicitly save it."},
  {"href":"/tools/productivity/wifi-qr","title":"WiFi QR Tool","category":"Tool","description":"Share a WiFi network as a QR code, without storing the password.","body":"WiFi QR Tool Share a WiFi network as a QR code, without storing the password. Builds the standard WIFI: QR payload from SSID, password, encryption type and hidden flag, then renders it as PNG or SVG. The password is used to render the image and is never written to the database; saving the result as a report stores only the SSID and encryption type."},
  {"href":"/tools/productivity/time-card","title":"Time Card Calculator","category":"Tool","description":"Clock-in/clock-out totals with breaks and overtime.","body":"Time Card Calculator Clock-in/clock-out totals with breaks and overtime. Calculates worked time from clock-in/clock-out pairs and breaks, in either 12- or 24-hour format, and applies the overtime rule you specify (daily or weekly thresholds)."},
  {"href":"/tools/productivity/colors","title":"Designer Colour Tools","category":"Tool","description":"Convert between HEX, RGB, HSL, HSV/HSB and CMYK.","body":"Designer Colour Tools Convert between HEX, RGB, HSL, HSV/HSB and CMYK. Converts a colour between HEX, RGB, HSL, HSV/HSB and CMYK, shows the preview, contrast ratio against black and white, and provides copy-ready values for each notation."},
  {"href":"/tools/productivity/reverse-image","title":"Reverse Image Search","category":"Tool","description":"Launch an image search with the engines you choose.","body":"Reverse Image Search Launch an image search with the engines you choose. Opens the reverse-image-search service you pick (Google Lens, TinEye, Bing Visual Search, Yandex Images) in a new tab. This tool performs no crawling or scraping of third-party engines: the search itself happens in your browser, under those services' own terms."},
  {"href":"/tools/productivity/image-ocr","title":"Image → Text (OCR)","category":"Tool","description":"Extract text from an image using a configured OCR provider.","body":"Image → Text (OCR) Extract text from an image using a configured OCR provider. Uploads an image to the administrator-configured OCR provider and returns the extracted text with a confidence estimate where the provider supplies one. No OCR provider configured means CONFIGURATION_REQUIRED — the platform does not guess at text."},
  {"href":"/tools/history","title":"Tool History","category":"Tool","description":"Your recent tool runs, with the metadata that was stored.","body":"Tool History Your recent tool runs, with the metadata that was stored. Lists your own tool runs (tool, target, time, status) and lets you clear them. Credentials, SMTP passwords, API keys, private keys, full card numbers and email contents are never stored in history."},
  {"href":"/tools/favorites","title":"Favorites","category":"Tool","description":"The tools you have starred.","body":"Favorites The tools you have starred. Shows your starred tools and lets you remove them. Favorites are per account."},
  {"href":"/tools/reports","title":"Saved Reports","category":"Tool","description":"Diagnostic results you chose to save, downloadable and deletable.","body":"Saved Reports Diagnostic results you chose to save, downloadable and deletable. Saves the exact result you saw (with credential-shaped fields stripped) so it can be downloaded, attached to a support ticket or compared later."},
  {"href":"/tools/monitors","title":"Monitoring","category":"Tool","description":"Scheduled SSL-expiry, DNS-record and email-configuration monitoring.","body":"Monitoring Scheduled SSL-expiry, DNS-record and email-configuration monitoring. Registers a monitor that the CloudHost247 worker evaluates on a schedule: SSL certificate expiry thresholds, specific DNS records whose value must not change, and the email authentication configuration (MX/SPF/DKIM/DMARC/BIMI). Notifications are delivered through the existing CloudHost247 notification system."},
  {"href":"/tools/barcode-generator","title":"Barcode Generator","category":"Tool","description":"Create 83 barcode types, including Code 128, EAN-13, UPC, QR Code and Data Matrix, as SVG, PNG or PDF.","body":"Barcode Generator Create 83 barcode types, including Code 128, EAN-13, UPC, QR Code and Data Matrix, as SVG, PNG or PDF. Encodes your data in any of 83 linear, 2D, GS1, postal and healthcare barcode types and returns vector SVG and PDF at the exact bar width you set, plus a PNG whose modules are whole pixels at the resolution you choose. A batch makes one barcode per line, a numbered series counts for you, and either can be laid out on label sheets. Nothing you enter is stored."},
  {"href":"/tools/label-designer","title":"Online Label Printing","category":"Tool","description":"Print asset tags, product, shelf, QR code and address labels on label sheets or a label printer.","body":"Online Label Printing Print asset tags, product, shelf, QR code and address labels on label sheets or a label printer. Choose a label template, fill in its fields and download a print-ready PDF: labels placed at true size on common A4 and US Letter label sheets, or one label per page for a label printer. A barcode keeps a bar width a scanner can read, or the label is refused with the reason. Nothing you enter is stored."},
  {"href":"/tools/vda-4902-label-generator","title":"VDA 4902 Label Generator","category":"Tool","description":"Fill in and print the 16-field VDA 4902 transport label at A5 or KLT size, with Code 39 barcodes.","body":"VDA 4902 Label Generator Fill in and print the 16-field VDA 4902 transport label at A5 or KLT size, with Code 39 barcodes. Draws the goods label used between automotive suppliers and plants: receiver, unloading point, delivery note, supplier, part number, quantity, package number, batch and the rest of the sixteen fields, with Code 39 barcodes that begin with each field’s data identifier (N, P, Q, 30S, V, S/M/G, H). Captions are available in English, German, French, Spanish and Portuguese."},
  {"href":"/tools/shipping-label-generator","title":"Shipping Label Generator","category":"Tool","description":"Make carrier-neutral 4 × 6 in and A6 parcel labels with a reference or SSCC barcode.","body":"Shipping Label Generator Make carrier-neutral 4 × 6 in and A6 parcel labels with a reference or SSCC barcode. Lays out sender, recipient, service, weight and package count on a 4 × 6 inch, A6 or 100 × 150 mm label and adds a Code 128 reference barcode or a GS1-128 SSCC, with one numbered label for each package. The result is a print-ready PDF for label printers or plain sheets. Addresses are processed in memory and never stored."},
  {"href":"/tools/qr-business-card-designer","title":"QR Code Business Cards","category":"Tool","description":"Design a business card with a QR Code or Data Matrix that saves your contact to a phone.","body":"QR Code Business Cards Design a business card with a QR Code or Data Matrix that saves your contact to a phone. Builds a business card from your name, role and contact details and encodes the same details as a vCard or MeCard in a QR Code or Data Matrix. Download a print-ready PDF as a single card or a sheet with cut marks, SVG artwork and a .vcf contact file. Contact details are processed in memory and never stored."},
  {"href":"/tools/qr-code-maker","title":"QR Code Maker","category":"Tool","description":"Make QR codes that open a link, join Wi-Fi, save a contact, start a WhatsApp chat, add an event or set up a SEPA payment.","body":"QR Code Maker Make QR codes that open a link, join Wi-Fi, save a contact, start a WhatsApp chat, add an event or set up a SEPA payment. Choose what the code should do when a phone scans it and fill in ordinary fields: a web address, a Wi-Fi network, a contact, an email, a call, a text or WhatsApp message, a calendar event, a map location, a social media profile or a SEPA bank transfer. The tool writes the format phones recognise and returns the code as PNG, SVG and PDF, as a QR Code, Data Matrix or Aztec Code. The code holds the content itself, so it never expires and scans are not tracked. Nothing you enter is stored."},
  {"href":"/tools/barcode-scanner","title":"Barcode Scanner","category":"Tool","description":"Scan barcodes and QR codes with your camera or from an image, and export what you scanned.","body":"Barcode Scanner Scan barcodes and QR codes with your camera or from an image, and export what you scanned. Reads twenty-one barcode types, including QR Code, Data Matrix, Code 128, Code 39, EAN-13, UPC-A and UPC-E, with a phone or laptop camera or from a picture. Each scan is added to a list you can copy or download as a CSV file. On the scanner page the decoding happens in your browser: the camera picture and your images are not uploaded. The API reads a barcode from an uploaded PNG, in thirteen of those types."},
  {"href":"/faq#faq-1","title":"What is CloudHost247?","category":"FAQ","description":"CloudHost247 is a professional web hosting and cloud solutions provider offering secure, reliable, and high-performance hosting, domain registration, and managed IT services for individuals, businesses, and organizations worldwide.","body":"What is CloudHost247? CloudHost247 is a professional web hosting and cloud solutions provider offering secure, reliable, and high-performance hosting, domain registration, and managed IT services for individuals, businesses, and organizations worldwide."},
  {"href":"/faq#faq-2","title":"What services do you offer?","category":"FAQ","description":"We provide: - Shared, VPS, and Dedicated Hosting - Cloud Hosting Solutions - Domain Registration and Management - Website Security and SSL Certificates - Managed Server Support - Email Hosting - Data Backup and Recovery Services","body":"What services do you offer? We provide: - Shared, VPS, and Dedicated Hosting - Cloud Hosting Solutions - Domain Registration and Management - Website Security and SSL Certificates - Managed Server Support - Email Hosting - Data Backup and Recovery Services"},
  {"href":"/faq#faq-3","title":"How do I create an account?","category":"FAQ","description":"Click Create Account, and follow the on-screen instructions. Once you complete the registration, you'll receive an email confirmation.","body":"How do I create an account? Click Create Account, and follow the on-screen instructions. Once you complete the registration, you'll receive an email confirmation."},
  {"href":"/faq#faq-4","title":"How can I pay for my services?","category":"FAQ","description":"We accept multiple payment methods, including: - Credit/Debit Cards - PayPal - Bank Transfers - Cryptocurrency (Bitcoin, Ethereum where applicable)","body":"How can I pay for my services? We accept multiple payment methods, including: - Credit/Debit Cards - PayPal - Bank Transfers - Cryptocurrency (Bitcoin, Ethereum where applicable)"},
  {"href":"/faq#faq-5","title":"Do you offer refunds?","category":"FAQ","description":"Yes, we have a Refund Policy that applies to eligible services. Refund requests must be submitted within the specified refund period stated in our Refund Policy.","body":"Do you offer refunds? Yes, we have a Refund Policy that applies to eligible services. Refund requests must be submitted within the specified refund period stated in our Refund Policy."},
  {"href":"/faq#faq-6","title":"How do I cancel my account or services?","category":"FAQ","description":"You can cancel your account by: - Logging into your Dashboard and submitting a cancellation request - Contacting our support team through the Contact us","body":"How do I cancel my account or services? You can cancel your account by: - Logging into your Dashboard and submitting a cancellation request - Contacting our support team through the Contact us"},
  {"href":"/faq#faq-7","title":"How do I request data deletion?","category":"FAQ","description":"Refer to our Data Deletion Instructions. Send your account details through the Contact us, and we'll process your request in accordance with our Data Protection Standards.","body":"How do I request data deletion? Refer to our Data Deletion Instructions. Send your account details through the Contact us, and we'll process your request in accordance with our Data Protection Standards."},
  {"href":"/faq#faq-8","title":"Do you keep my personal information safe?","category":"FAQ","description":"Absolutely. We follow strict Data Protection Standards that comply with GDPR, CCPA, and other regulations. Your data is encrypted, stored securely, and never sold to third parties.","body":"Do you keep my personal information safe? Absolutely. We follow strict Data Protection Standards that comply with GDPR, CCPA, and other regulations. Your data is encrypted, stored securely, and never sold to third parties."},
  {"href":"/faq#faq-9","title":"Do you provide 24/7 customer support?","category":"FAQ","description":"Yes, our support team is available 24/7/365 via: - Contact us - Live Chat (on our website) - Support Tickets in the Client Area","body":"Do you provide 24/7 customer support? Yes, our support team is available 24/7/365 via: - Contact us - Live Chat (on our website) - Support Tickets in the Client Area"},
  {"href":"/faq#faq-10","title":"How do I transfer my website to CloudHost247?","category":"FAQ","description":"We offer free migration assistance for most hosting plans. Simply contact our support team with your current hosting details, and we'll handle the transfer for you.","body":"How do I transfer my website to CloudHost247? We offer free migration assistance for most hosting plans. Simply contact our support team with your current hosting details, and we'll handle the transfer for you."},
  {"href":"/faq#faq-11","title":"What happens if my website gets hacked?","category":"FAQ","description":"If your website is compromised, our security team can assist with malware removal, security patches, and restoration from backups (if backups are active on your account).","body":"What happens if my website gets hacked? If your website is compromised, our security team can assist with malware removal, security patches, and restoration from backups (if backups are active on your account)."},
  {"href":"/faq#faq-12","title":"Where can I read your full policies?","category":"FAQ","description":"All our policies, including Privacy Policy, Terms & Conditions, Refund Policy, Cookie Policy, and Data Protection Standards, are listed on our Legal & Policy Center.","body":"Where can I read your full policies? All our policies, including Privacy Policy, Terms & Conditions, Refund Policy, Cookie Policy, and Data Protection Standards, are listed on our Legal & Policy Center."},
];

